# Typography and color

Typography should carry much of the visual identity. Use scale, weight, line length, and wrapping to create energy before adding decoration.

## Typography

- Inspect existing fonts and brand assets before choosing type.
- Do not select Inter or Geist merely because they are available.
- Use a readable body face and a distinctive display strategy appropriate to a local recreation organization.
- A second family is optional; first use size, weight, width, spacing, and case well.
- Keep body copy at a comfortable measure.
- Use intentional heading wraps; avoid accidental orphan words.
- Do not automatically center headings.
- Avoid tiny uppercase labels, repeated eyebrow text, oversized italic-serif shortcuts, and display headlines so large that they crowd the mission or CTA off the first screen.
- Maintain a logical semantic heading order independent of visual size.

## Color

- Derive the final palette from the approved Friends of Recreation logo and existing brand assets.
- Do not invent final brand colors when the logo or approved palette is unavailable.
- Once approved, define semantic CSS variables and use them instead of arbitrary component values.
- Give colors roles such as canvas, ink, brand, action, supporting field, and border.
- Use one dominant field and restrained supporting accents rather than every brand color at once.
- Verify WCAG 2.2 AA contrast in actual states and backgrounds.

## Shape and effects

- Establish a small radius scale from the brand's geometry.
- Do not reach automatically for `rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`, `shadow-lg`, or hairline-border-plus-wide-shadow cards.
- Use borders, radius, and shadows only when they explain grouping, elevation, or interaction.
- Prefer semantic design tokens over arbitrary values. Exact one-off values are acceptable when faithfully implementing a deliberate approved composition.

Treat shadcn/ui as behavior and accessibility infrastructure, not as the site's visual language. Restyle primitives to fit the project and do not wrap ordinary content in `Card` by default.

